# Edge RateGuard

Standards-based HTTP rate limiting middleware built on the Web Fetch `Request` and `Response` primitives with zero Node.js-specific dependencies.

## Installation

```bash
npm install @forgehub/edge-rate-guard
```

## Middleware Usage

```javascript
import { createRateGuard } from '@forgehub/edge-rate-guard';

const limiter = createRateGuard({
  windowMs: 60_000,
  maxRequests: 120,
  keyGenerator: (req) => req.headers.get('cf-connecting-ip') || 'anonymous',
  standardHeaders: true
});

export default {
  async fetch(request) {
    const verdict = await limiter.check(request);
    if (!verdict.allowed) {
      return verdict.toTooManyRequestsResponse();
    }
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }), {
      headers: verdict.headers
    });
  }
};
```

## Response Headers

Automatically attaches IETF draft-compliant headers (`RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining`, `RateLimit-Reset`, and `Retry-After`).
